" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=11 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317570/field-1" "q-317570/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317583/field-1/1d8e4d4ca05809b4ff03e4ab5c8a87e8ac0dbc724f449ca6244d0db5e7d4cddb" :answer/id #uuid "d356e6d9-2f05-51ee-a259-073969094204" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317583/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c638c59-e340-5dbe-984f-08f55dad2115" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317583/field-1/1d8e4d4ca05809b4ff03e4ab5c8a87e8ac0dbc724f449ca6244d0db5e7d4cddb" :answer-field/choices ["q-317583/field-1/1d8e4d4ca05809b4ff03e4ab5c8a87e8ac0dbc724f449ca6244d0db5e7d4cddb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317583/field-2/6cc821050cc2dc7e7576ca2cf117d9f022929f456b903a4ab38ceb667e41194e" :answer/id #uuid "1e6fb009-90d6-59ee-9108-0f0192ccb211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317583/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c364a68-57f2-54a7-9b72-eaa196ce06be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317583/field-2/6cc821050cc2dc7e7576ca2cf117d9f022929f456b903a4ab38ceb667e41194e" :answer-field/choices ["q-317583/field-2/6cc821050cc2dc7e7576ca2cf117d9f022929f456b903a4ab38ceb667e41194e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317583" :question/id #uuid "7423fd02-a062-5332-9ecb-3b402fa82521" :question/math-academy-id "q-317583" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+0y=10 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=10 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317583/field-1" "q-317583/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4505"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/cdadd8a9c68f58c4d8434e658d4acffeba524850f361fcd3d6fe3524b3d781a1.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/35104266eb5a086bef0536640ec1310532cc136a251049a1adcfe4418ef0ef89.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/aa4de061ca95088763e7e5fec289dbd2e5bd298e8986ef6660617ea0ba227821.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/10781c0f9183c793e3f2de287ede937e764d942767ecc9b64942dc338c1e1307.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4506"] :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y=0 \\\\ x-y=-8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/648952bc6e093c08ff29215fce21fe115ab81e9fc3d8b423772123eae31237f3.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/c1f203be0770c298d9c2c75ccfbfb30354cb314ed75c8b05f6639e5633ca7442.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/aa4de061ca95088763e7e5fec289dbd2e5bd298e8986ef6660617ea0ba227821.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/75aed8c54a2ec274def967802cbd3b67d0fad3358e676b02cf52e1e8d2cbe0d7.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4507"] :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/6f0ddb43928e0d9f52ca2fe0f0ab578adfa986cba8179746bd34a50a1a7c506b.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
